I'm out of healing crystals!

33
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:54,590
Inna!

34
00:02:54,673 --> 00:02:56,280
Inna! Inna!

35
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:58,010
Ah!

36
00:02:58,093 --> 00:03:09,200
Inna…

37
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,440
Pina!

38
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:46,660
Don't leave me all alone here!

39
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,080
Pina!

40
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,456
What's that feather?

41
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:57,930
It's Pina.

42
00:03:58,013 --> 00:03:59,720
My best friend.

43
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:03,967
You're one of those
beast tamers, aren't you?

44
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:05,917
I'm sorry.

45
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,118
If I got here sooner, I
could have saved your friend.

46
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:10,970
No.

47
00:04:11,053 --> 00:04:11,883
It's all my fault.

48
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:16,261
I was stupid to think I could make
it through the forest on my own.

49
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:19,300
Thank you for saving me.

50
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:22,180
You did what you could. That feather.

51
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:26,019
Check and see if it has an
item name attached to it.

52
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:35,380
Hey, don't cry.

53
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,477
That means Pina's heart's still here.

54
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,619
There's a chance you can revive it.

55
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,580
No way, really? Mm-hmm.

56
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:47,997
On the south side of floor 47, There's a
field dungeon called the Hill of Memories.

57
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:52,433
I heard somewhere that the flower
growing at the top can revive familiars.

58
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,300
4.47, huh?

59
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,537
I'd offer to go get it for you.

60
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:02,757
All you'd have to do is pay for the trip.

61
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:06,877
The thing is, the flower won't bloom
unless the familiars' master's there.

62
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:09,431
Thank you so much for telling me about it.

63
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:12,597
If I work hard to raise my
level, then someday I could...

64
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:15,680
Sure, but the time limit's
three days to revive it.

65
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,470
No way.

66
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,320
It's all my fault.

67
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:23,000
I'm so sorry, Pina.

68
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:24,850
It's okay.

69
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,300
You have three days.

70
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,756
Take this equipment.

71
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:31,837
It should boost you five or six levels.

72
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:35,096
And if I tag along, I'm sure
everything will work out.

73
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:40,000
But why would you do all this for me?

74
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:46,652
I'll tell you, but only if you
promise not to laugh, okay?

75
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:48,860
I promise I won't.

76
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,390
All right.

77
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:55,348
It's because you look
like my little sister.

78
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,080
I'm sorry.

79
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,557
Mom, I know this isn't enough
cold to pay you back, but...

80
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:11,470
No, it's cool.

81
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,857
Besides, it works with why I'm here.

82
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:15,822
We'll be helping each other out.

83
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:17,450
Okay, then.

84
00:06:17,533 --> 00:06:18,520
My name's Silica.

85
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:19,700
My name's Kirito.

86
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:23,078
I guess we'll be working
together for a little while.

87
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:32,160
Hey, look! It's Silica!

88
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,797
It took you a long time to get back.

89
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,292
We were getting worried.

90
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:38,257
You want to team up with us?

91
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:40,577
We'll take you wherever you want to go.

92
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:43,280
That's really nice of you to offer, but...

93
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:49,062
Well, I've sort of already agreed
to be in a party with him, so...

94
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,240
Okay, later, bye!

95
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:58,285
I didn't mean to put you
on the spot like that.

96
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,817
Didn't know you had fans.

97
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:01,076
You must be popular.

98
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:02,530
No.

99
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:05,197
They don't take me seriously.

100
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:07,162
They want me to be their mascot.

101
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,357
Maybe they're right.

102
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:14,977
They call me dragon tamer and
I guess it went to my head.

103
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,860
Don't worry about it.

104
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,677
We'll make it in time!

105
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:20,590
Promise.

106
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:27,617
Do you live around here, Kirito?

107
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:29,237
I'm on floor 50.

108
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:32,297
It's kind of far, so I was
thinking of getting a room tonight.

109
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:35,337
If you stay, I'll take you
out for some cheesecake.

110
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,737
It's really good here.

111
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:38,620
Well, if it isn't silica.

112
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:43,212
Wow, you made it out of the forest alive.

113
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,618
Good for you, girl.

114
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:46,661
Something wrong?

115
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:49,100
Oh, no, nothing. Hang on.

116
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:51,577
What happened to your
little friend the lizard?

117
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:52,940
Did it run away?

118
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,800
Peanut died saving me.

119
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:58,500
But I'm gonna get Peanut back. Really?

120
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:02,117
I guess you'll be heading for
the Hill of Memories then.

121
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:05,318
I wonder if you'll be able
to clear it at your level.

122
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:07,080
Of course she will.

123
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:09,661
It's not that difficult to level.

124
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:13,080
Oh, God, this girl seduced another player.

125
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:16,797
No, it's not difficult, but
you don't look that strong.

126
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:17,710
Come on.

127
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:23,800
Why does she have to be so mean?

128
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:28,260
Well, is Sword Art Online your first MMO?

129
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:29,690
Uh-huh.

130
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:33,781
A lot of people's personalities
change when they play games online.

131
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:37,415
And some actually like playing
the game as the bad guy.

132
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,720
You see how our cursors are green?

133
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:44,477
Well, if you commit a crime against another
player, your cursor's gonna turn orange.

134
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,977
Then they become what's
called a red player.

135
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,500
The worst, also known as player killers.

136
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,291
They're all about murder.

137
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:53,420
They kill other players?

138
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:57,897
In a normal game, they roleplay as the
bad guy, have some laughs, and it's cool.

139
00:08:57,980 --> 00:09:00,860
But Sword Art Online isn't normal.

140
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:05,700
It's definitely not a game.

141
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:08,290
Kirito?

142
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:11,360
I'm sorry.

143
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:16,417
Well, I think you're good, so...

144
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:18,480
I mean, you saved me after all.

145
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:22,856
Looks like you cheered me up instead.

146
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:24,980
Thank you, Silica.

147
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,886
Wow, where the heck is
our cheesecake already?

148
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:32,880
Excuse me!

149
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:35,182
Our dessert hasn't shown up yet!

150
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:45,320
I wonder if he'd laugh if I told
him I wanted to talk some more.

151
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:48,420
Silica, you still awake?

152
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:50,380
Kirito!

153
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:55,308
I forgot to tell you some stuff about
floor 47, but it can wait till tomorrow.

154
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:56,257
No, now's fine!

155
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:59,458
Actually, I was just thinking
I should ask you about…

156
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,960
That was so close.

157
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,240
What's up? Something wrong?

158
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,317
No, nothing.

159
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:13,400
What's that thing do, Kirito?

160
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:15,240
It's a mirage sphere.

161
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,580
It's pretty.

162
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:30,820
This is the town area of 447
and that's the Hill of Memories.

163
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:33,648
I was thinking if we
take this route, we can

164
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:35,970
What's wrong?

165
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:37,490
Who's there?

166
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,720
Um, who was it?

167
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:43,400
An eavesdropper.

168
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:44,640
But they can't.

169
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:47,617
I mean, you can't hear through
a door unless you knock first.

170
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:50,477
But if your listening skill
is high enough, you can.

171
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,619
It takes practice.

172
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:53,477
Not that many players have it.

173
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:56,000
Why would they want to listen to us? Huh?

174
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,510
Wow!

175
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,700
This place is like a dream!

176
00:11:10,220 --> 00:11:11,050
I know.

177
00:11:11,133 --> 00:11:13,257
The whole floor is covered in flowers.

178
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,811
That's why they call it the Flower Garden.

179
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:26,890
Couples!

180
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:34,150
Silica?

181
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:35,450
Nothing!

182
00:11:35,533 --> 00:11:36,477
Sorry to keep you waiting.

183
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:39,900
What's wrong? Nothing.
Nothing at all. Come on.

184
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:42,490
Okay.

185
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:47,320
What's that for?

186
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:51,677
If anything bad happens while we're in
here, I'm gonna tell you to warp out, okay?

187
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,407
When I do, use this crystal.

188
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:55,581
You can jump to any town with it.

189
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:57,540
But... No buts. Use it.

190
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,030
I understand.

191
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:03,401
Let's get going.

192
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:07,502
If we take this path, it'll lead
us right to the Hill of Memories.

193
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:18,570
Um, Kirito...

194
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:28,500
Calm down!

195
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:30,506
That thing's not that strong!

196
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:33,820
Oh, Jimmy, don't save me!
But don't look! Save me!

197
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:34,790
But don't look!

198
00:12:34,873 --> 00:12:36,440
That'll be...difficult.

199
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:38,870
Darn you!

200
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,920
Look me down! Now!

201
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:56,876
Do you see anything?

202
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,000
Not really.

203
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:05,880
I hope you don't mind me asking,
but what's your sister like?

204
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:07,532
Why do you want to know?

205
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:10,140
Well, you said I looked like her.

206
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:15,660
I know it's not polite to ask about
your real life, but what's she like?

207
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:19,820
I call her my little sister,
but she's really my cousin.

208
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:23,737
We were raised like
brother and sister since

209
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:26,232
we were babies so I doubt she even knows.

210
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:30,137
But I know and I guess that's
the reason I avoided her.

211
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:32,877
Our grandfather's really strict.

212
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:36,157
When I was eight he made us
take classes at the local

213
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:39,817
kendo dojo but after a
couple years I stopped going.

214
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:42,277
Grandpa beat the hell out of me for that.

215
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,597
That's awful.

216
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:47,937
Anyway then my sister stood up
for me and told him to stop.

217
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:51,537
She said she'd train hard
for both of us and she did.

218
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:52,797
She trained hard.

219
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:56,297
She even made it to the
nationals. She did. How awesome?

220
00:13:56,380 --> 00:14:00,837
Yeah I've always felt guilty
for putting her through that.

221
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,117
I wouldn't doubt it if she hates me.

222
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,277
God knows she could have
been doing something else.

223
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:09,697
Maybe that's why I wanted
to help you in a weird way.

224
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:11,937
It makes me feel like I'm paying her back.

225
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:13,617
There it is.

226
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:17,277
If you don't mind me saying you're wrong.

227
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:19,077
I don't think she hates you at all.

228
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:22,457
She wouldn't work that hard
for you if she didn't like you.

229
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:25,237
Promise and I bet she even loves kendo.

230
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:29,100
There you go again making me feel.

231
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:32,377
Maybe you're right.

232
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:33,640
Man, I hope so.

233
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:37,110
Okay, then.

234
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:39,000
I'm gonna do my best, too.

235
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:45,970
Kiriko!

236
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:02,980
Is that reviving flower around here?

237
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:04,360
Yeah, over there.

238
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,355
Go ahead, pick it up.

239
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:38,114
You sure it'll bring Pina back to life?

240
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:39,390
Uh-huh.

241
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:40,640
I'm so glad.

242
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:43,777
There's a bunch of strong
monsters lurking around here.

243
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:45,817
Let's revive it when we get back to town.

244
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:48,076
I'm sure Pina would want it that way.

245
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:49,510
Okay.

246
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:57,300
Is something wrong?

247
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:59,357
Whoever's hiding out there, come out.

248
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,270
Now.

249
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:05,810
Rosalia?

250
00:16:05,893 --> 00:16:08,357
If you saw through my
hiding skill so easy,

251
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:11,499
your detection skill must
be really high, Swordsman.

252
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:16,957
Ooh, it looks like you were successful
getting your hands on the Name Flower.

253
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:17,981
Congratulations.

254
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:21,160
Now, hand it over before you get hurt.

255
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:23,068
What are you talking about?

256
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:25,700
No one's handing anything over, Rosalia.

257
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,020
Not to you.

258
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:28,378
Or the Orange Gill.

259
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:30,300
Or should I say Titan's hand?

260
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:32,108
You're their leader, right?

261
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:33,370
Nice.

262
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,665
But Rosalia's cursor is green.

263
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:36,940
It's an easy trick.

264
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:39,616
The green members find their victims.

265
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:43,797
Then, they lure them straight to
the orange players for the ambush.

266
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:47,960
That was one of your pals last night
eavesdropping on us, wasn't it?

267
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:52,197
Then, the reason you were in that
party with me and the others was to...

268
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:54,060
How perceptive.

269
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:58,987
I was observing their strength and watching
them earn all that beautiful money.

270
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:05,157
You were who I was excited about and
I was so sad when you left the party.

271
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:08,181
But then you told me you
were getting a rare item!

272
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:12,037
What I want to know is if you knew
about us, why did you bring her here?

273
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:15,649
Are you dumb or does she have
you wrapped around her finger?

274
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,537
Nope, you're wrong both times.

275
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:21,860
See, I've been looking
all over for you, Rosalia.

276
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,168
What are you talking about?

277
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:28,560
Remember ten days ago, you attacked
a guild called the Silver Flags?

278
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:29,856
The leader survived.

279
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:30,960
Ford didn't.

280
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:33,400
Oh, the losers with no money.

281
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,537
Their leader went back and forth,

282
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:38,437
from the warp point to the
front lines morning till night,

283
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:43,057
and with tears in his eyes, he begged
everyone he met to avenge his dead friends.

284
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:44,980
But he didn't want you killed.

285
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:47,780
No, he wanted you to go to prison.

286
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:50,920
Do you have any idea how he felt?

287
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:52,600
Can't say I do.

288
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:55,000
Only idiots take this seriously.

289
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:57,137
So what if we kill someone here?

290
00:17:57,220 --> 00:18:00,161
There's no proof dying
here means you're dead IRL.

291
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:04,194
Anyway, it's time you started
worrying about yourselves.

292
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:15,857
Kirito, there's too many of them.

293
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:17,337
We should get out of here.

294
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:18,320
No, it's okay.

295
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:20,477
You'll be safe if you stay here.

296
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,736
Keep the crystal handy till I say so.

297
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:24,520
Okay, but...

298
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:26,970
Kirito!

299
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:28,730
Kirito?

300
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:32,240
Dressed in black, one-handed, no shield.

301
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:35,020
Holy crap, it's the Black Swordsman.

302
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,560
Rosalia, that guy.

303
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:40,157
He's the beater who plays
solo on the front lines.

304
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,677
He's with the assault team.

305
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:42,920
No way he is.

306
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:46,857
Why would someone from the assault
team be all the way down here?

307
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:51,100
Go on, take him out and take
everything he owns. Die!

308
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:02,400
I've got to save him. He won't last.

309
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:08,580
What's going on?

310
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:17,580
What the hell, you idiots?

311
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:18,980
Kill him already!

312
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,680
410 seconds, give or take.

313
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:27,304
That's about the total damage the
seven of you can inflict on me.

314
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,400
I'm level 78.

315
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:32,360
I got 14,500 HP.

316
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:37,400
My battle healing skill auto-regenerates
600 points every 10 seconds.

317
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:41,632
We could stand here all day
and you wouldn't get anywhere.

318
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:43,960
That's not possible. Wanna bet?

319
00:19:44,420 --> 00:19:47,420
If your numbers are high
enough, you're invincible.

320
00:19:47,780 --> 00:19:50,780
Miss that use leveling
systems are unfair that way.

321
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:55,037
My client spent his entire fortune on this

322
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:57,497
warp crystal and he'll
get his money's worth.

323
00:19:57,580 --> 00:20:00,345
It's been set to the
coordinates of the prison.

324
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:03,251
And I'm sending all of you bastards there.

325
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:07,976
Well, I'm green, and if you
hurt me, you'll go orange.

326
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:15,680
I'm a solo player, got it.

327
00:20:16,260 --> 00:20:19,907
I don't care if I have to play
as orange for a couple of days.

328
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:27,700
I'm really sorry, Silica.

329
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:31,238
This whole time I was using
you as bait to catch him.

330
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:34,831
I thought you'd be scared if
I told you the truth about me.

331
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,224
I could never be scared of you.

332
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:40,826
Because you're a good person.

333
00:20:43,180 --> 00:20:45,180
Um, do you really have to go?

334
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:49,277
Yeah, I've been away from the
front lines for five days.

335
00:20:49,360 --> 00:20:50,680
I need to get back.

336
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:55,260
I think it's Koya with the assault team.

337
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:58,641
I could try for a hundred
years and never make it.

338
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:03,357
Um, I...

339
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:05,440
You know, levels are just numbers.

340
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:09,052
And a person's strength in
this world is just an illusion.

341
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:13,956
Sure, it's cool and all, but there
are more important things than that.

342
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:16,878
We should meet up in the real world.

343
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,057
That would be cool.

344
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:20,375
because I like having you as a friend.

345
00:21:22,660 --> 00:21:24,160
Okay, we will.

346
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:25,520
I promise.

347
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:29,220
Well, ready to revive Pina? Yeah!

348
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:47,780
Pina, when you get back, I'll have
lots of stuff to tell you about.

349
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:52,720
About the amazing adventure I had.

350
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:03,460
And about this one day, when I got
to have my very own big brother.

351
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:22,417
I heard the sound of the

352
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:27,440
money that was a little late.

353
00:22:30,560 --> 00:22:32,360
But once again, I'm strong.

354
00:22:34,100 --> 00:22:40,997
And now, I'm so proud of the truth.

355
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:46,140
But the fact that the
fact that the reality is.

356
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:51,797
We can't wait to

357
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:55,857
see the future!

358
00:22:55,940 --> 00:22:57,797
We can't wait to see the future!

359
00:22:57,880 --> 00:23:04,080
We can't wait to see this.

360
00:23:04,660 --> 00:23:07,460
Before we open the world?

361
00:23:36,280 --> 00:23:37,180
Next time.

362
00:23:37,460 --> 00:23:38,872
Murder in the safe zone.
